<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Offers up as rain slows harvest.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Offers up as rain slows harvest.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail and truck soymeal offers were steady to firmer on Wednesday as rains slowed soybean harvest in Kansas, Missouri and Nebraska, several U.S. Midwest brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis is very uncertain because it's raining every day and we can't (harvest) beans,&quot; a Kansas City broker said.</p>
<p>Rains were expected to linger in the western U.S. Midwest through Saturday, further delaying harvest and straining tight new crop supplies.</p>
<p>Dealers said end-users continued to buy hand to mouth in expectation of lower prices after harvest.</p>
<p>But delays meant end-users had to buy more to cover nearby demands.</p>
<p>&quot;Inventories are just tight right now,&quot; an Illinois dealer said. &quot;Everybody is waiting till the last minute to buy meal.&quot;  </p>
